From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: ranges, the selection and the main story answer ITextRange2

Office's React Native text boxes go through a RichEdit's ITextDocument2:
Word's start screen box ("Describe the document you'd like to write")
reads and replaces its text through Range2, GetSelection2 and
GetMainStory, which 1490 left as stubs -- typing went after the
placeholder instead of replacing it.

- A range and the selection answer ITextRange2 (and the selection
  ITextSelection2): their vtables continue past ITextRange's and
  ITextSelection's methods. GetCch, GetText2, SetText2, GetChar2 and
  GetDuplicate2 work, through the object's own ITextRange methods; the
  rest of ITextRange2 is not there yet (E_NOTIMPL), as before.
- ITextDocument2's Range2, GetSelection2 and GetMainStory give them.
- ITextStory (include/tom.idl had only its name: its methods in the
  order of the public interface definition): the main story -- its type,
  index, text, SetText and GetRange -- through a range of its own, which
  knows when the document is gone.

Wine's richole tests: 181430, no failures, as before.

Gate: test/textrange2-gate.sh. Mutants SG_MUTANT_RICHED_NO_RANGE2,
SG_MUTANT_RICHED_NO_STORY, SG_MUTANT_RICHED_SETTEXT2_NOOP.
